# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.tp3-full -- GLM-5.3-Flash FULL-SCOPE EXL3, TP=3 + expert parallel +
# DFlash2 k=7 + the vision tower. This is production configuration 13.
#
# It is env.tp3.example with eight lines changed for the full-scope checkpoint,
# and six more for the vision tower. Everything not repeated here -- the NCCL
# notes, the memory ladder, the block-size reasoning -- is in env.tp3.example
# and applies unchanged; read that file first.
#
# TEXT-ONLY FALLBACK (production configuration 12). This file serves images and
# video. To go back to text only, six lines change and nothing else:
#   LANGUAGE_MODEL_ONLY=1
#   drop HAREM_VISION=1 and CUDA_EXL3_PACKED_MAPPING from EXTRA_ENV
#   drop the four --mm-* arguments from EXTRA_ARGS
#   TP3_DIR / OVERLAY_DIR -> the tree without patches/vision/
#   FASTLOAD_DIR -> the text-only sidecar (a DIFFERENT directory; the tower
#     changes the tensor name list and the identity check is exact equality,
#     so the two sidecars can never be the same one)
# Keep the text-only env under a name that says what it is. docs/18.
#
# ONE COPY PER NODE, derived on that node, never copied between nodes. On our
# cluster it is produced by tracks/tp3/patches/mk-env-tp3full.sh, which sed-derives
# it from each node's own .env.tp3 and therefore keeps NODE_RANK, HOST_IP,
# OVERLAY_DIR, NCCL_MESH_PLUGIN_DIR and CHAT_TEMPLATE_HOST correct by
# construction. See envs/README.md.
#
# Placeholders to replace:
#   @NODE_RANK@    0 on the head node, 1 on worker-1, 2 on worker-2
#   @HOST_IP@      this node's own management address
#   @HEAD_IP@      the head node's management address (same on all three)
#   @IFACE@        the management network interface name
#   @HOME@         this node's home directory
#
# Consumed by scripts/start-tp3.sh. Launch order: rank 2, then 1, then 0.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NODE_RANK=@NODE_RANK@
HOST_IP=@HOST_IP@

MASTER_ADDR=@HEAD_IP@
MASTER_PORT=29531
GLOO_IFACE=@IFACE@
FABRIC_PREFIX=
TRANSPORT=mesh

# --- Parallelism ------------------------------------------------------------
NNODES=3
TP_SIZE=3
# Still mandatory. Full scope quantizes the dense path, not the routed experts:
# they are 4-bit EXL3 in both checkpoints, moe_intermediate_size is still 2048,
# and 2048/3 is still not an integer. docs/03, docs/13.
ENABLE_EP=1

# --- Model and drafter ------------------------------------------------------
# CHANGED: the full-scope checkpoint and its own sidecar. Both sidecars are
# relative symlink trees, so each is mounted at its own host path (identity
# mount) and the launcher refuses anything else. Do NOT set MODEL_PATH.
# Build this sidecar with tracks/tp3/patches/pad-tp3full.py -- it writes the padded
# config.json AND the rewritten quantization_config.json that carries the packed
# mapping. patches/tp3/pad-tp3.py does not, and the load then fails. docs/13.
MODEL_HOST_PATH=/var/tmp/glm-5.3-flash-turboderp-4.05bpw-tp3
MODEL_LINK_TARGET=/var/tmp/glm-5.3-flash-turboderp-4.05bpw
DRAFT_HOST_PATH=/var/tmp/dflash2-draft-tp3
DRAFT_LINK_TARGET=/var/tmp/dflash2-draft

SPEC_METHOD=dflash
SPEC_TOKENS=7

# --- Serving ----------------------------------------------------------------
PORT=8001
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=glm-5.3-flash
QUANTIZATION=exl3
ATTENTION_BACKEND=CUSTOM
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8
MAX_MODEL_LEN=1000000
MAX_NUM_SEQS=8
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=2048
ENFORCE_EAGER=0
# CHANGED in production 13. 0 makes start-tp3.sh pass
# `--skip-mm-profiling --limit-mm-per-prompt ...` instead of `--language-model-only`,
# which is what lets an image be submitted at all. It does NOT on its own make the
# tower load -- that needs patches/vision/ and the two EXTRA_ENV lines below.
# Set it back to 1 for the text-only fallback (production configuration 12).
# The launcher's own limit string is overridden by the EXTRA_ARGS copy: argparse
# _StoreAction, last one wins, and EXTRA_ARGS is appended after. docs/18.
LANGUAGE_MODEL_ONLY=0
REASONING_PARSER=deepseek_r1
REASONING_EFFORT=low
CPUSET=5-9,15-19

# --- Memory -----------------------------------------------------------------
# 0.87 is PRODUCTION 11 (6 September 2026), the top of a ladder climbed rung by
# rung in one session: 0.85, 0.87 and 0.88 all pass; 0.90 is rejected because the
# head node pages 1.5 GB out and reads 143 MB back under load, while every
# concurrency level is still inside its band -- the aggregate tok/s is the LAST
# place that failure shows. 0.88 passes too and was not taken: it leaves 1.86 GiB
# of MemAvailable on the head node against 0.87's 3.49, and that headroom is what
# anything running beside the engine lives in. Every 1 % of this fraction costs
# about 1.2 GiB of host memory here.
#   KV pool: 5,674,931 at 0.83 -> 6,363,636 at 0.87, +12.1 %.
# PRODUCTION 12 takes this to 0.88, the rung the ladder measured, passed and
# declined -- declined on diagnostic headroom, not on any measurement. At 0.88
# the head node keeps about 1.5-3.2 GiB of MemAvailable under load, so the
# budget for anything running BESIDE the engine is ~2 GiB and a profiling run
# has to stop the engine first. 0.89 has never been measured. 0.90 is rejected.
# WATCH swap TRAFFIC (si/so per second from vmstat), not swap used and not
# MemFree: swap used sits at ~0.04 GiB at every rung including the failing one,
# and MemFree is mostly reclaimable page cache on a unified-memory part.
# results/memory/ladder-6sep.md, docs/07 section 6, docs/00 section 11.2.
# Roll back one rung by changing this line alone -- it is NOT part of the
# fast-load manifest identity, so it never costs a dump boot.
# PRODUCTION 13 does NOT move this. Turning the vision tower on was expected to
# cost a rung, because the head node is the one that runs the API server and the
# multimodal frontend adds 1.2-1.4 GiB to its resident set. A 0.87 arm was
# prepared and never run: the worst-case stress -- a 1M-token request, a C8
# round, and a 4-image + 2-video request sent WHILE the C8 round ran -- produced
# no error, no OOM, no slowdown outside the bands, MemAvailable never below
# 1.47 GiB, and swap that SETTLED at 1.57 GiB instead of growing. No KV pool was
# given up for a harm that measurement could not find. docs/18 section 9.
GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.88
SETTLE_MIN_GIB=112

# --- Image ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHANGED, and this one is not optional. The padded-load path needs cuda-exl3
# f3e3090 (a padded output dim is accepted when the pad is whole 128-blocks,
# with svh allocated zeroed; and the row-parallel suh load copies what exists
# and zeros the rest) AND 754421f (the vocab loaders fill a prefix instead of
# copy_ing an unpadded slice into a padded parameter). On 62f53e6 or 5903248 the
# boot raises "EXL3 weights cannot be zero-extended" in create_weights; on
# f3e3090 alone it passes that gate and then dies on a copy_ shape mismatch in
# _vocab_loaders. tracks/tp3/patches/check-padload-tp3.py reads all three
# capabilities out of the installed source in the prelude and exits 23 before a
# byte of weight is read. docs/13 section 7.
IMAGE=exl3-zeus:754421f

# OVERLAY_DIR: the GB10 top-k overlay (patches/indexer-overlay/). From production
# 11 this must be a copy with sm_12x item 2 PRE-APPLIED on the host, because the
# launcher bind-mounts sparse_attn_indexer_kpool.py from here READ-ONLY and the
# prelude cannot write it from inside the container. From production 12 the
# indexer-workspace patch lands on the SAME file, so the copy carries TWO
# pre-applied hunks. Make the copy, run patches/patch-kpool-init.py and
# patches/indexer-workspace/patch-indexer-workspace-tp3.py against it once, and
# point this at the copy; the prelude will then report "already applied" for
# that file in both blocks. Verify with `diff -r` against the overlay it came
# from: exactly one file differs, by exactly those hunks.
OVERLAY_DIR=@HOME@/exl3-zeus/tp3prefix/overlay-prod11
# Pin CHAT_TEMPLATE_HOST to zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash @ 690b7052 (4 Sep 2026),
# 10,950 bytes, sha256 0c4099f3382d6c92700dfb99725025360966fd73032f0ecf32377c0d9e6309c5
# -- only this revision carries the tool-calling fixes, and its clear_thinking
# default is the one both launchers already guard (docs/14 section 9.11 /
# 9.12). Verify with:
#   python3 scripts/verify-chat-template.py "$CHAT_TEMPLATE_HOST"
# (script merged from PR #5).
CHAT_TEMPLATE_HOST=@HOME@/exl3-zeus/chat_template.jinja
NCCL_MESH_PLUGIN_DIR=@HOME@/exl3-zeus/nccl-mesh-patched2
# PROFILER_DIR=/cache/prof

# --- The patch tree ---------------------------------------------------------
# CHANGED. /opt/harem-tp3 and /start.sh are mounted from here. The production
# tp3/ directory is deliberately untouched: its file list is the fast-load
# manifest identity, and adding a single file to it has already refused a
# production boot twice. docs/08 section 4, docs/09 section 11.2.
#
# NAMING. The launcher directory and the patch-tree directory are two things.
# The systemd unit's WorkingDirectory/ExecStart point at the launcher, which the
# docs write as tp3full/; TP3_DIR and OVERLAY_DIR below point at the directory
# holding the patches, the prelude and the overlay. The docs use tp3full/ for
# both for brevity; ours is named after the configuration, as here. Any name
# works -- set TP3_DIR to wherever you put the patch tree.
#
# PRODUCTION 13 points this at a tree that additionally contains everything in
# tracks/tp3/patches/vision/: patch-vision-tp3.py, three model-free gates, the
# fixture videos the geometry gate reads, and a prelude carrying the vision
# block. That is a different file list, so it is a different fast-load identity
# and a different sidecar -- which is the whole reason the promotion cost one
# dump boot. Keep the text-only tree in place beside it: with it and the kept
# sidecar, the rollback is one environment file and no dump boot.
# tracks/tp3/patches/vision/README.md.
#
# 8 September: the tree in production is `tp3prefix`, which is the vision tree
# plus patch-prefixhit-tp3.py and patch-kpooltail-tp3.py. Same reasoning as
# above -- two more patch files means a different fast-load identity and its own
# sidecar. The vision tree and its sidecar stay on disk beside it as the
# rollback pair. tracks/tp3/patches/prefix-hit-and-kpool-tail/README.md.
TP3_DIR=@HOME@/exl3-zeus/tp3prefix

# --- Environment passed into the container ----------------------------------
# HAREM_SM12_ITEMS=pdl,kpool is PRODUCTION 11: the sm_12x correctness set, three
# of the four findings of Zeuss5/cuda-exl3 issue #6. `pdl` turns Programmatic
# Dependent Launch OFF on sm_12x, where upstream's `major >= 9` gate had it on for
# a part it was never qualified on; `kpool` initialises the K-pool top-k buffer to
# -1 and bounds its reader from above, so a short row's allocator residue cannot
# expand into a real token index. Both were measured free before they were adopted
# (results/kernels/sm12-stack-patches-ab.md) and again as part of this
# configuration. Unset the variable and the tree is production 10 byte for byte.
# DO NOT also set HAREM_PDL_SM12=1 -- that restores the upstream gate and undoes
# item 1. Item 4 is not here on purpose: tracks/tp3/patches-optional/sm12/.
# NOTE: adding patch-*.py files to TP3_DIR changes the fast-load manifest
# identity, so this costs one dump boot. Change the memory rung in the same boot.
#
# HAREM_EXL3_FULLSCOPE=1: one knob for S1+S2+S3+A9+A10. With it
# unset the patched image is upstream byte for byte and still serves the
# routed-experts-only checkpoint, because the patch reads the knob at run time
# and takes the split decision from the checkpoint rather than the environment.
# That is the one-line rollback for this whole arm. docs/13 section 3.
#
# TWO ADDITIONS IN PRODUCTION 13, both for the vision tower. Drop both for the
# text-only fallback; with HAREM_VISION unset the tree is configuration 12 byte
# for byte, because every vision anchor reads the knob at run time.
#
# HAREM_VISION=1 arms the six anchors of patches/vision/patch-vision-tp3.py.
#
# CUDA_EXL3_PACKED_MAPPING gives back the ONE packed-mapping entry that
# HAREM_EXL3_FULLSCOPE's A2 shadows. A2 replaces the class's whole
# packed_modules_mapping, which is where the inherited Glm4v `qkv_proj` entry
# lived; cuda-exl3 merges this environment value UNDER the class mapping
# (config.py:112-125, :381-386), so it can only ADD. Without the union 24 of the
# 99 vision linears do not resolve and get_quant_method falls back to BF16
# SILENTLY -- a tower that loads clean and answers wrong. NO SPACES in the JSON:
# EXTRA_ENV is word-split. docs/18 section 3.2.
#
# HAREM_PREFIX_HIT=1 and HAREM_KPOOL_TAIL_FIX=1 were promoted on 8 September
# 2026 and are production settings from here on. They need the patch tree that
# carries patch-prefixhit-tp3.py and patch-kpooltail-tp3.py (both applied
# unconditionally by the prelude; the environment decides the behaviour), and
# because the patch scripts join the fast-load identity hash, that tree needs
# its OWN sidecar -- FASTLOAD_DIR below points at it. Drop both variables and
# the image is upstream on those paths byte for byte.
# tracks/tp3/patches/prefix-hit-and-kpool-tail/, docs/11 sections 2.32-2.34.
#
# HAREM_KDA_FLASHKDA=1 was promoted on 10 September 2026: GLM-5.3-Flash's KDA
# chunked prefill runs through the fused vllm._flashkda_C kernel instead of the
# ten-kernel Triton chain. Sustained prefill +6.5 %, TTFT at 7K -5.1 %, decode
# and KV pool unmoved, four gates full. Unset or 0 is upstream byte for byte --
# and the knob is NOT part of the fast-load identity, so dropping it is a
# one-line rollback that keeps the sidecar. The patch FILE is part of the
# identity, which is why FASTLOAD_DIR below is renamed again.
# tracks/tp3/patches/flashkda/, results/gates/flashkda-ab-10sep.md, docs/11 section 2.35.
#
# HAREM_GLM47_FAILCLOSED=1 was adopted on 11 September 2026 (issue #7): the glm47
# tool-call parser refuses a malformed tool call instead of salvaging it, which is
# what ends the malformed-tool-call cascade that swallows whole turns in long
# agentic sessions. It is listed here for the record rather than for effect --
# this knob DEFAULTS ON, so an unset or missing variable is still fail-closed;
# only HAREM_GLM47_FAILCLOSED=0 goes back to upstream, byte for byte. It is the
# one knob in this file whose default is not upstream, because here the upstream
# default is the bug. Like the FlashKDA knob it is not part of the fast-load
# identity, so flipping it is a restart; the patch FILE is, which is why
# FASTLOAD_DIR below is renamed again.
# tracks/tp3/patches/glm47-failclosed/, results/gates/failclosed-11sep.md,
# docs/14 section 9.13.
EXTRA_ENV="HAREM_GLM47_FAILCLOSED=1 HAREM_KDA_FLASHKDA=1 HAREM_PREFIX_HIT=1 HAREM_KPOOL_TAIL_FIX=1 HAREM_DISABLE_PERSISTENT_TOPK=1 NCCL_MAX_NCHANNELS=8 HAREM_SW_BLOCK_SIZE=256 HAREM_DRAFT_KV_DTYPE=fp8 CUDA_EXL3_TUNE_CACHE=/cache/tune NCCL_MESH_LINKS_PER_PEER=0 NCCL_MESH_MIN_RNR_TIMER=1 NCCL_MESH_PTR_CUDA=1 NCCL_MESH_FLUSH=1 HAREM_TILELANG_FAILLOUD=1 HAREM_EXL3_FULLSCOPE=1 HAREM_SM12_ITEMS=pdl,kpool VLLM_DEBUG_WORKSPACE=1 HAREM_INDEXER_WS_MODE=bound HAREM_VISION=1 CUDA_EXL3_PACKED_MAPPING={\"qkv_proj\":[\"q_proj\",\"k_proj\",\"v_proj\"]}"

# HAREM_VISION_VIDEO_LIMIT is optional and defaults to 2. It is only read when
# HAREM_VISION=1, and it is what VS7 substitutes for the inherited
# get_supported_mm_limits() -> {"video": 1}, which silently clamped
# --limit-mm-per-prompt through a min(). docs/18 section 4.5.

# CUDA_EXL3_DEBUG_NAMES=1 is a boot gate rather than a setting: since cuda-exl3
# 807d798 it logs at warning and reports the modules that RESOLVED as well as
# those that stayed BF16, with running tallies. Expected on this checkpoint:
# 203 EXL3 / 113 bf16, and nothing heavy in the "-> unquantized" list. Reading
# it is the acceptance gate; leaving it on costs a few log lines. docs/09.
CUDA_EXL3_DEBUG_NAMES=1

# --- Launcher arguments -----------------------------------------------------
# CHANGED, and note the SINGLE quotes. This checkpoint's inlined quantization
# config carries no tensor_storage, so cuda-exl3 has to be pointed at the
# standalone file -- which the sidecar rewrote to carry the packed mapping as
# well. In double quotes the shell eats the JSON's own quotes; the JSON must
# also contain NO SPACES, because start-tp3.sh word-splits these arguments.
# From cuda-exl3 fba9f27 onwards the same JSON can travel in
# CUDA_EXL3_PACKED_MAPPING instead -- same no-spaces rule.
#
# FOUR ADDITIONS IN PRODUCTION 13. Drop all four for the text-only fallback.
# Every JSON below has NO SPACES for the same word-splitting reason.
#
#   --mm-encoder-tp-mode data
#       The tower is REPLICATED on every rank rather than sliced. At TP=3
#       nothing in it divides by three -- not the 16 heads, not the 4096 MLP,
#       not the merger's 4096/10240 -- so slicing would be four padded shapes
#       and a new pad audit to save 0.28 GiB/rank. The model declares
#       supports_encoder_tp_data = True (glm4_1v.py:1782). Cost: 0.416 GiB per
#       rank, and one large item runs on ONE rank while the other two wait.
#       AT TP=2 THIS FLAG IS NOT NEEDED -- everything divides. docs/18 section 2.
#
#   --mm-processor-kwargs {"max_pixels":12544000,"max_image_tokens":8000}
#       TWO KEYS, TWO JOBS, and for three rounds only the wrong one was set.
#       max_image_tokens is THE BRAKE: it is what reaches the video processor.
#       max_pixels does NOT -- Glm5NextVideoProcessorKwargs does not declare it
#       and the engine logs that it is ignored -- but it is still what vLLM's own
#       budget estimate reads, and dropping it takes the per-item budget from
#       10,242 tokens to 32,242 and charges the difference to the KV pool.
#       MEASURED on a 1080p clip: no kwarg 10,764 vision tokens; max_pixels only
#       10,764 (unchanged); max_image_tokens=8000 -> 7,788. Images are
#       BIT-IDENTICAL under all three, because the checkpoint already budgets
#       images at 8,000 tokens. Unbraked, a ceiling video is ~960,000 patches and
#       ~14.6 GiB of SwiGLU buffer in ONE forward -- the tower does not chunk.
#       8,000 tokens/item = 0.49 GiB peak, and the encoder takes ONE item at a
#       time (max_encoder_items_per_batch = 1). docs/18 section 5.
#
#   --limit-mm-per-prompt {"image":4,"video":2}
#       Per request. The video:2 half needs VS7: upstream declares
#       {"image":None,"video":1} and processing/context.py takes the min(), so
#       without the patch this line silently means 1. A third video is refused
#       with HTTP 400 and the engine stays up (VS6).
#
#   --mm-processor-cache-gb 0
#       HOST memory, and it defaults to 4 GiB on the rank that runs the API
#       server. Off, idle MemAvailable there went 1.10 -> 3.42 GiB. What it
#       costs: a request that sends the same image twice runs the tower twice.
#       docs/18 section 9.
#
# ONE ADDITION ON 12 SEPTEMBER 2026, and it goes INSIDE the --hf-overrides JSON
# above rather than beside it -- one object, two keys, still no spaces.
#
#   "index_topk":8192
#       The checkpoint declares 2048. With index_kpool 4 that makes the per-row
#       top-k 512, and past ~32k tokens of agentic context the sparse indexer
#       stops retaining enough of the history for BYTE-EXACT copying of
#       look-alike strings: tool-call path arguments come back with a single
#       character slipped (depo -> dego), with context spliced onto the end, or
#       with markup leaked into the value. Prose is unaffected and every
#       single-turn gate passes, which is why this took a bisection to find.
#       MEASURED, 30-turn replay at 30-41k prompt tokens, bad turns out of 30
#       (full prefill / prefix-cache reuse): 2048 -> 11/7, 4096 -> 6/4,
#       8192 -> 2/3. Speculative decoding off, FlashKDA off, bf16 KV and the
#       grammar off all left it in place, so none of those is the cause.
#       WHAT IT COSTS: a 7K-prompt prefill reading 1,868 -> 1,366 tok/s (-27 %),
#       per-turn prefill on the replay about +11 %; decode, KV pool and boot
#       time unmoved. That is the largest price any change here has carried --
#       read results/gates/index-topk-8192-12sep.md section 7 before copying it.
#       DO NOT RAISE IT FURTHER: 16384 and 65536 die in worker init with
#       CUDA error: invalid argument, and "index_topk":null (dense MLA) is
#       refused by the EXL3 attention backend ('non-sparse not supported').
#       This is NOT an environment knob, and it is part of the fast-load
#       identity -- see FASTLOAD_DIR below. docs/14 section 9.15.
EXTRA_ARGS='--block-size 256 --enable-ep-weight-filter --safetensors-load-strategy eager --no-enable-flashinfer-autotune --hf-overrides {"quantization_config_file":"/var/tmp/glm-5.3-flash-turboderp-4.05bpw-tp3/quantization_config.json","index_topk":8192} --mm-encoder-tp-mode data --mm-processor-kwargs {"max_pixels":12544000,"max_image_tokens":8000} --limit-mm-per-prompt {"image":4,"video":2} --mm-processor-cache-gb 0'

# --- Fast-load sidecar ------------------------------------------------------
# CHANGED: a new directory name. Four inputs to the manifest identity moved at
# once (checkpoint, sidecar config, patch tree, image), so the previous sidecar
# cannot be used under any circumstances -- and reusing the NAME would have
# overwritten production 8's sidecar during the dump, because the launcher
# mounts this directory read-write in dump mode. Take one FASTLOAD_MODE=dump
# boot (about 590-620 s here), pass the gates, then switch to load (272 s at
# production 12, of which 80 s is weights). docs/08.
# Production 12 renamed this again for the same reason: the indexer-workspace
# patch changed the manifest identity, and keeping the name would have
# overwritten production 11's sidecar -- the one that makes the rollback above
# a single cp instead of another dump boot.
#
# PRODUCTION 13 renames it a third time, and here the rename is not a
# convention, it is forced. The tower becomes part of the model, so the sidecar
# gains 596 tensor names and 0.42 GiB (5,858 -> 6,454 names, 50.24 -> 50.66
# GiB), and harem_fastload._restore compares the name set by EXACT EQUALITY:
# a tower-carrying engine REFUSES the text-only sidecar, loudly, which is the
# correct behaviour. Reusing the name would have overwritten the text-only
# sidecar during the dump and destroyed the one-file rollback. Take one
# FASTLOAD_MODE=dump boot (454 s here), then switch to load: 247 s by hand,
# 244 s under the unit, and 318 s for a whole-cluster reboot. Disk: 53 GB per
# node, and BOTH sidecars fit -- 546-547 GB free per node afterwards.
# docs/08, docs/18 section 8.
#
# 8 September: the prefix-hit / K-pool tail tree gets its own sidecar again,
# for the same reason and at the same price -- one dump boot (495 s) and 53 GB
# per node. Boots from it measured 251 / 265 / 266 s under the unit. The vision
# sidecar is kept, so the rollback is still one environment file and no dump.
#
# 10 September: renamed a FIFTH time, for patch-flashkda-tp3.py -- one more
# patch-*.py in the directory is one more hash in the identity, and there is no
# "registered but switched off" state that avoids it. One dump boot (394 s),
# 53 GiB per rank, then load at 181 s. The prefix sidecar
# (/var/tmp/glm53-exl3-prefix-r{0,1,2}) is kept untouched as the way back, so
# the rollback is still one environment file. Disk: 546 G -> 493 G free per node,
# and CHECK THAT BEFORE YOU START -- a dump into a full disk is an outage.
# And read docs/14 section 10.6 before pointing this at a new name: the
# ExecStartPre sidecar gate used to demand a MANIFEST even in dump mode, which
# made a new directory unbootable and cost 18 minutes. The shipped
# motor-onkosul-exl3.sh is the fixed one; an older copy of yours is not.
#
# 11 September: patch-glm47-failclosed-tp3.py makes it a SIXTH rename, for the
# same reason -- one more patch-*.py is one more hash in the identity, and there
# is no "registered but switched off" state that avoids it. Point this line at a
# NEW directory, dump once (380 s on our nodes), then FASTLOAD_MODE=load. The
# flashkda sidecar is kept as the way back, so the rollback is one environment
# file and no dump. tracks/tp3/patches/glm47-failclosed/README.md section 4.
#
# 12 September: renamed AGAIN, and this time NOT for a patch file. "index_topk"
# in --hf-overrides above is part of the manifest identity -- harem_fastload
# compares hf_overrides inside the engine (docs/08 section 4) -- so a launcher
# argument invalidated the sidecar exactly as a patch-*.py would. The first try
# with FASTLOAD_MODE=load was refused outright: "harem-fastload: sidecar was
# written for a different model configuration". Point this line at a NEW
# directory, dump once (about 6 minutes here), then FASTLOAD_MODE=load, which
# boots in 170 s. 53 GB per rank. The xgrammar sidecar is kept as the way back,
# so the rollback is one environment file and no dump. AND WHEN YOU EXPERIMENT
# with this override rather than adopt it, leave FASTLOAD_MODE EMPTY -- a full
# load is about 5 minutes and it beats a refused boot.
# results/gates/index-topk-8192-12sep.md section 8.
FASTLOAD_DIR=/var/tmp/glm53-exl3-flashkda
FASTLOAD_MODE=load
FASTLOAD_VERIFY=32
FASTLOAD_SHARD_BYTES=2147483648

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rolling back to production 8 is one file: keep the old env under a name that
# says what it was (ours is .env.tp3.bak-prod8-62f53e6) and start with
# ENV_FILE pointing at it. That reverts the checkpoint, the image, the patch
# tree and the sidecar in one move, because all four are named in this file.
